Subject: [PATCH] hwdb: remove supported 06cb:00be from unsupported allowlist

The pinned synatlsmoc fork already registers 06cb:00be but leaves the same
device in the unsupported-device allowlist. The hwdb generator warns about
this duplicate and aborts under the test suite's G_DEBUG=fatal-warnings.
The autosuspend.hwdb file already lists it only under synatlsmoc.

diff --git a/libfprint/fprint-list-udev-hwdb.c b/libfprint/fprint-list-udev-hwdb.c
--- a/libfprint/fprint-list-udev-hwdb.c
+++ b/libfprint/fprint-list-udev-hwdb.c
@@ -67,7 +67,6 @@ static const FpIdEntry allowlist_id_table[] = {
   { .vid = 0x06cb, .pid = 0x00a8 },
   { .vid = 0x06cb, .pid = 0x00b7 },
   { .vid = 0x06cb, .pid = 0x00bb },
-  { .vid = 0x06cb, .pid = 0x00be },
   { .vid = 0x06cb, .pid = 0x00cb },
   { .vid = 0x06cb, .pid = 0x00da },
   { .vid = 0x06cb, .pid = 0x00dc },
